.TH TRANSFORM 1
.SH NAME
transform \- the fourth row of the transformation matrix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/transform
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Transform
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Transform.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
"This highlights the 4th dimension of the transformation matrix which is
used for storing translations (shifts) in matricies so they can be
combined with a matrix multiplication."
.PP
It is
.IR scrollbars (1)'s
map of 2048 square with 256 trees, put under a matrix that three sliders
drive: the first turns the whole map, the third scales it, and the second
spins every tree about its own centre without touching the map matrix at
all, because the sprite call takes its own angle.
.PP
The scroll range is the arithmetic worth reading.  A map rotated and
scaled needs a window from minus scale times height times the sine of the
angle across to scale times width times its cosine, because the corners
move; the program recomputes that every frame from the slider rather than
tracking a bounding box.  The translation goes in the fourth column of
the same matrix, which is the point: shifting is a multiplication like
any other, so scroll, rotation and scale compose into one matrix applied
once per sprite.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Move a slider, or drag a scroll bar
.TP
.B arrows
Scroll
.TP
.B "any other key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/transform.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
